+# F2 Data Plane — Migration Pack #1 (re-scoped)
+
+Date: 2026-09-11
+Branch: `feat/f2-data-plane` (worktree `.worktrees/f2-data-plane`, based on `origin/main` @ 044fcc4)
+Issue: `product-suite-5q8` (PS tracker)
+
+## Purpose
+
+F2 was specced in June against a greenfield `infra/db/` plane with a neutral runner and Supabase-CLI-replacing codegen. None of that is how the repo actually grew. The plane lives in `packages/db` (Drizzle, hand-authored SQL, migrations 0000-0021), the runner is `scripts/migrate-database.mjs`, and the CI gate is `DB Contract / db-contract`. What F2 still owes is the ladder pieces F3 and the Phase 1 lanes need, plus three infra gates that disagree with each other.
+
+Scope A (approved in session): build the genuinely missing pieces where the plane lives, skip legacy-only value migrations, fix the drift items.
+
+## Success criteria
+
+1. Migration `0022` ships: `project_teams`, `checks.project_id` + at-most-one-parent constraint, proposals candidate idempotency columns + partial unique index, `connections` (user|workspace scope, encrypted credentials), item visibility (`org`|`restricted`) + `visibility_grants`, `playbooks` + `projects.playbook_ref`.
+2. `bun run check:migration-parity` passes with a real `meta/0022_snapshot.json` (chain hop from 0019, the gate's documented tolerance). The `SNAPSHOTLESS_MIGRATION_BASELINE` list is untouched.
+3. Contracts extended (Check parent, Visibility, Playbook, Connection, ProjectTeam) with drift-guard tests green.
+4. platform-api enforces visibility on work-item and check reads; a route test proves a restricted item is hidden without a grant and visible with one. Check writes accept a project parent and reject both parents at once.
+5. Infra drift fixed: `drizzle-kit generate` script removed from `packages/db/package.json` (and its config reference), expected-pending pins updated to `0018-0022`, `database-authority.json` suffix policy aligned and bound by a test.
+6. Local lanes green in the worktree: `packages/db` tests, `verify:platform-api`, `test:repo-tooling` (baseline flake list below).
+7. Production apply of 0018-0022 via the human-gated deploy job, then re-fetch `__drizzle_migrations` to prove the tags landed. This is an out-of-band step, not CI.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Legacy-only value migrations (`timeline_items` fold, milestones rebind, `workspaces.phase` retirement, status drop). The legacy Supabase DB is deleted at Phase 2 and the new plane never had those tables.
+- Historical snapshot chain repair for 0012-0018, 0020, 0021 (separate workstream, referenced as issue `1c8d790e`).
+- Connections HTTP routes / connect UI (Agent lane builds the connect flow on top of the table + crypto module).
+- Team-scoped visibility (`org`|`team`|`restricted` per DESIGN). No team-membership model exists in the codebase, so `team` cannot be enforced honestly today. Follow-up when memberships land.
+- Agent / automation / connector / MCP catalog tables — later packs.
+- Codegen replacing Supabase typegen. Contracts are hand-authored with drift guards; no pain to fix yet.
+
+## Approach selected
+
+One migration (`0022`) for the whole pack, one PR. Table naming follows the current vocabulary: the DESIGN `project_departments` junction is built as `project_teams` because PR #79 promoted departments to the `teams` table. Proposals idempotency is reconciled onto the DESIGN 4-tuple via nullable `source_*` columns and a partial unique index; existing dedup mechanisms (`meeting_promotions`, `applied_from_proposal_uniq`, `memories_source_proposal_uniq`) stay as second guards. Visibility ships as `org | restricted` with grants; `team` waits for memberships. Connections ship schema + contract + an AES-256-GCM crypto module, no routes.
+
+### Snapshot strategy (the one hard constraint)
+
+The parity ratchet requires a `meta/0022_snapshot.json` and forbids both hand-writing one and extending the baseline. `drizzle-kit generate` works against the holed chain: probed on 2026-09-11, it emitted snapshot `9285dcfa-...` with `prevId` = 0019's id — exactly the chain hop the gate documents. Its generated SQL is unusable (it re-diffs 0020/0021 changes), so:
+
+1. Make every `schema.ts` edit first.
+2. Run `drizzle-kit generate` once; keep only `meta/0022_snapshot.json`; discard the generated SQL and journal entry.
+3. Hand-author `0022_f2_data_plane.sql` + the matching `_journal.json` entry (idx 22).
+4. Prove with `bun run check:migration-parity`.
+
+This breaks AGENTS §6.1 (`generate` is forbidden) for one bounded step, deliberately and visibly, because the ratchet demands a snapshot and no sanctioned generator exists. Recorded in the PR body. The SQL stays hand-authored.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Host-neutral SQL: no `auth`/`storage` schemas, no RLS, app-layer authz. Must satisfy `packages/db/test/sql-firewall.test.ts`.
+- Migration style: `--> statement-breakpoint` separators, head comment explains why, journal `idx` is 0-based.
+- Contracts are hand-authored across `enums.js`, `work-items.js`, `index.d.ts`, `contracts/*.json`, kept in sync by `work-items.test.ts` / `enums.test.ts`.
+- Visibility enforcement is one shared predicate used by list and detail reads; fail closed (restricted without grant = not found).
+- No hook, lint, test, or gate bypass anywhere.
+
+## Edge cases (decisions)
+
+- Check parents: neither parent allowed (loose check), both parents = 400 at the API and a DB check constraint (`num_nonnulls(...) <= 1`) as the backstop.
+- Restricted visibility: the caller sees the item when a `visibility_grants` row exists, or when they are the assignee. Without that, an item set to restricted by its creator would vanish for everyone.
+- Proposals: `source_candidate_id IS NULL` rows are exempt from the unique index, so agent/reflection proposals (no candidate concept) keep working. Meeting ingest populates the 4-tuple from the candidate id it already holds.
+- Connections: owner is the creating user for `user` scope; workspace scope is stored but admin gating lands with the connect flow.
+- Snapshot `when` timestamp is set by hand to the day of generation.
+
+## Rollback (per migration-spec discipline)
+
+`0022` down path, in reverse order: drop FK + column `projects.playbook_ref`; drop `playbooks`; drop `visibility` columns; drop `visibility_grants`; drop `connections`; drop the proposals index + 4 columns; drop the checks constraint + index + `project_id`; restore `checks.work_item_id NOT NULL` (fails if loose or project-parented checks exist — delete them first); drop `project_teams`; drop the two enums. Pins and scripts revert in the same commit. Production has no outside users yet, so data loss on rollback is acceptable and stated here.
+
+## Technical Research
+
+### DRY / reuse
+
+- Migration + schema pattern: `packages/db/src/schema.ts` + hand-authored `NNNN_name.sql` + journal + snapshot; tests assert schema metadata via `getTableConfig` and read raw SQL with `readFileSync` (`packages/db/src/schema.test.ts:152-160,193-209`).
+- Route pattern: Hono + `clerkAuth` + tenant-scoped raw SQL; write routes go through `recordWrite` provenance (`apps/platform-api/src/routes/checks.ts`, `provenance/record-write.ts`).
+- Visibility precedent: memory lanes pin `visibility = 'org'` / `visibility = 'private' AND owner_user_id = $n` in SQL (`apps/platform-api/src/agent/memory-retrieval.ts:390-429`); item visibility follows the same shape.
+- Idempotency precedent: partial unique indexes already carry dedup (`0014_work_item_applied_from_proposal_partial.sql:11`, `0011_memory_source_proposal_uniq.sql:9`).
+- No encryption utility exists (zero hits for AES/cipher); the connections module is new.
+
+### Blast radius
+
+- `checks.work_item_id` nullability: route reads/writes (`routes/checks.ts:13,54-63,89-137,181,234`), route tests, contract `Check` (`index.d.ts:894-905`, `work-items.js:204-213`, `work-items-core.json:96-105`), web repository filter (`apps/platform-web/src/data/work-items/network-repository.ts:160-204`). Python backend and `packages/sdk` have zero checks consumers.
+- `work_items.department` stays untouched (deprecated column with live consumers in domain + write allowlist).
+- Proposals writers: `proposals/repository.ts:145` (shared helper), `agent/tools.ts:160,205`, `agent/reflection.ts:120`, raw insert `meeting/ingest.ts:188`.
+- Expected-pending pins: `scripts/migrate-database.mjs:339-343,722`, `scripts/migration-evidence.mjs:206-210`, plus their tests.
+
+### OWASP (what applies here)
+
+| Risk | Applies | Mitigation in this pack |
+|---|---|---|
+| A01 Broken access control | Yes | Visibility predicate on every ladder read; fail-closed 404; grants checked server-side. |
+| A02 Cryptographic failures | Yes | AES-256-GCM, random IV per record, key from env only (`CONNECTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY`), no plaintext logging. |
+| A03 Injection | Yes | Parameterized SQL only; constraint and column names are static constants. |
+| A04 Insecure design | Yes | Idempotency enforced in the DB, not the app; XOR parent rule at DB + API. |
+| A09 Logging/monitoring | Low | Reuse existing route error logging; never log encrypted payloads or keys. |
+
+### TDD scenarios (minimum set)
+
+1. Happy: create a check with `project_id` only; create one with `work_item_id` only; both 201.
+2. Error: create a check with both parents or a foreign parent → 400/404; DB constraint rejects a direct both-parents insert.
+3. Edge: restricted work item hidden from a caller without a grant (404), visible with a grant; assignee still sees it.
+4. Idempotency: replaying the same meeting candidate insert hits the partial unique index and is skipped, not duplicated.
+5. Crypto: round-trip encrypt/decrypt; tampered ciphertext and wrong key both fail closed.
+
+### Alternatives considered
+
+- Extend `SNAPSHOTLESS_MIGRATION_BASELINE` for 0022: rejected, it is exactly the gate-weakening the ratchet exists to stop.
+- Rebuild the whole snapshot chain first: rejected as separate workstream, not needed for a valid chain hop.
+- Name the junction `project_departments`: rejected in favor of `project_teams`, the vocabulary the codebase already uses.
+
+## Ambiguity policy
+
+Use the 7-dimension rubric scoring per the /dev decision gate. >= 80% confidence: proceed and document. < 80%: stop and ask.
